course: dictionary
lesson: 6822
title: Checking a story about animals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many people repeat the story that ostriches bury their heads in the sand to hide. This is a myth, a false story that people keep telling. A good scientist checks a story before repeating it.
explain: The context gives you the clue. «Ostriches do not bury their heads in the sand; to hide they lie flat with their necks along the ground.» So a real ostrich hides by lying flat, not by digging.
explain: An ostrich is a very large bird from Africa. It cannot fly, but it runs very fast on its long, strong legs. When you read a fact about animals, ask: does this match what I know, and can I check it?
fact: An ostrich is the biggest bird in the world.
fact: An ostrich cannot fly, but it runs very fast on its long, strong legs.
fact: An ostrich lays the biggest eggs of any bird.
fact: Each ostrich foot has 2 toes.
fact: An ostrich turns its eggs in the nest with its beak.
exercise: What is an ostrich? | A tall tree that grows in the desert | *A very large bird from Africa that cannot fly | A small fish that lives in the sea
exercise: «Ostriches do not bury their heads in the sand.» Is this a myth or a fact? | Fact, because it is in every book | Fact, because they dig holes to hide | Myth, because they cannot run at all | *Myth, because it is a false story that people repeat
exercise: Which statement about an ostrich is true? | It has three toes on each foot | *It lays the biggest eggs of any bird | It can fly high over the trees | It is a small bird from Europe
test: How many toes does each ostrich foot have? | *Two | One | Four | Three
test: How does a real ostrich hide from danger? | It buries its head in the sand | It climbs a tall tree | *It lies flat with its neck along the ground | It flies away fast
exam: Why is the story about ostriches burying their heads a poor fact to repeat? | *Because it is a myth, and a good scientist checks a story first | Because ostriches are very small birds | Because it is a true story from Africa | Because ostriches cannot run
